{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.channelAverage_eq_zero'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.channelAverage_eq_zero'","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L262-L267","doc":"The same statement in the form it is used: equal weights on values that sum\nto zero contribute nothing, whatever the weight is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.channelAverage_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.channelAverage_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L254-L260","doc":"The three-channel average of the reversal **vanishes identically** when the\nsymmetric and alternating weights are equal — which they are in the corpus's own\ndecomposition, `w_sym = w_alt = q²/(q⁴+4q²+1)`\n(`docs/audits/2026-06-17-hecke-channel-chirality-binding.md`).  Uses only that\nthe alternating value is the negative of the symmetric one\n(`CrossingReversalParity.alternating_eq_neg_symmetric`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.k3_ratio_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.k3_ratio_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L243-L252","doc":"**The block's two halves are different numbers for every `q > 1`** — the\n`k = 3` narrative does not derive the `k = 2` formula.  Scope (b) for exactly\nthat reading; the invariant is `(q²-q+1)(q²+q+1) ≠ q(q²+1)` away from `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.alpha_gt_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.alpha_gt_half","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L233-L241","doc":"`1/2 < α` for every real `q > 1`: `α - 1/2 = (q-1)²(q+1)²/(2(q²+1)²) > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.alpha_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.alpha_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L226-L231","doc":"`α < 1` for every real `q ≠ 0`: `1 - α = 2q²/(q²+1)² > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.k3_ne_k2_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.k3_ne_k2_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L216-L222","doc":"The two halves differ by `(q²-q+1)(q²+q+1)/(q(q²+1))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.k3Value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.k3Value","kind":"def","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L213-L214","doc":"The `k = 3` reversal value, `q³ - q⁻³` — the block's narrative half. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.zD_trace_eq_alpha_mul_baseline","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.zD_trace_eq_alpha_mul_baseline","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L204-L209","doc":"**Under the canonical `z_D` the same construction gives `α` times the\nbaseline** — a model flavour split scaled by `α`, which is `< 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.baselineX_eq_augmentation_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.baselineX_eq_augmentation_trace","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L198-L202","doc":"**The block's displayed baseline is exactly the augmentation's Markov\ntrace**, dressed by the block's own `ℏ_q²/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.baselineX_eq_hbarSq_symValue_div_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.baselineX_eq_hbarSq_symValue_div_three","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L190-L196","doc":"The displayed baseline is the `k = 2` form: `X_baseline = ℏ_q²(q²-q⁻²)/3`.\nThis is the identity that locates the block's formula at `k = 2`, against its\nnarrative's `k = 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.hbarOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.hbarOf","kind":"def","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L183-L184","doc":"`ℏ_q = 1 - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.baselineX","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.baselineX","kind":"def","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L180-L181","doc":"The block's displayed baseline coupling `X_baseline(q) = (q-1)²(1-q⁻⁴)/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.markovReversal_zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.markovReversal_zD","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L173-L178","doc":"**At `z_D` the Markov trace is `α` times the augmentation's**, exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.alphaOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.alphaOf","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L169-L171","doc":"The ratio between the two admissible cells, `α = (q⁴+1)/(q²+1)²`.  This is\nthe same `α` as the 2026-09-08 `Q_β` ruling's augmentation-to-`z_D` factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.zD","kind":"def","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L166-L167","doc":"The convention-D Markov parameter `z_D = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.markovReversal_augmentation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.markovReversal_augmentation","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L158-L164","doc":"**At the augmentation `z = q` the Markov trace IS the symmetric-channel\nvalue**, exactly.  No approximation, no prefactor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.symValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.symValue","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L154-L156","doc":"The symmetric-channel value of the reversal, `q² - q⁻²`.  Matches\n`CrossingReversalParity.symmetricValue`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.markovReversal_eq_h_mul_bondSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.markovReversal_eq_h_mul_bondSum","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L147-L152","doc":"The trace is `h` times the sum of the two like-pair bond letters\n`b_pp = z` and `b_nn = z - h` (`BondLetterIdentification.tr_bond_interp` at\n`t = 0` and `t = 1`).  Nothing beyond the corpus's own letters enters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.markovReversal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.markovReversal","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L139-L145","doc":"The Markov trace of the `k = 2` crossing reversal, at Markov parameter `z`.\n\nDerivation, using nothing but `tr(1) = 1` and `tr(σ) = z`:\n`σ² - σ⁻² = h·(σ + σ⁻¹)` (`CrossingReversalParity.reversal_two`) and\n`σ + σ⁻¹ = 2σ - h` (`inv_eq`), so the element is `2hσ - h²` and its trace is\n`2hz - h²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.hOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovCrossingReversal.hOf","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovCrossingReversal.lean#L136-L137","doc":"`h = q - q⁻¹`, the Hecke deformation parameter. ","signatureChunk":0}]}